-- §3 head projection + §7 single-evaluator law at an EFFECT-CARRYING impl head —
-- the #1618 DRAIN. Permanent home of `test/must_fail_fixtures/
-- 1618-effect-carrying-impl-head-cannot-build/`, which pinned the broken behaviour.
--
-- WAS: the two head projections DISAGREED. `typecheck.headTyconTy` matched only
-- `TyCon`/`TyTuple`, so a `TyEffect` head answered None and this impl landed in the
-- `noneHeadTag` bucket; eval's and `core_ir_lower`'s `headTycon` STRIPPED the effect
-- to the inner head `Int`. The front end therefore resolved the call and the EMITTER
-- could not find what it had resolved:
--   `check --json` -> {"diagnostics":[]}, exit 0
--   `run`          -> 2, exit 0                                     (CORRECT)
--   `build`        -> exit 1, no binary:
--      runtime error [E-PANIC]: no impl of method 'sz' for type '__none__'
--
-- There is no overlap here to be rejected for and nothing ambiguous: ONE interface,
-- ONE impl, ONE call. The only impl of `Sz` matching the receiver is this one, so
-- `sz 0` is its body — 2 — which `run` already printed. The defect was never the
-- value; it was that `build` could not reach the impl.
--
-- ⚠️ SO THE LOAD-BEARING CELL OF THIS ROW IS THE **BUILD** ARM, not the value.
-- `check` and `run` were both already correct pre-fix and their cells pass on a
-- compiler that never had this bug and on one that still does. Section 1's
-- `ALL_EXACT` mode is what makes the row discriminate: it requires `build` to
-- ACCEPT and its stdout to be byte-identical to `run`'s and to the pinned `2`, so a
-- regression that puts the effect-carrying head back into the `__none__` bucket
-- fails on the build cell alone. This is exactly the check/run-agree-build-diverges
-- blindness §7 exists for, and the reason a value-only reading of this row would
-- be vacuous.
--
-- ⚠️ ONE IMPL BLOCK, so Section 4 does not derive a permutation pair for this file —
-- correctly: there is no declaration order to be free of. Its sibling drain,
-- `s3-fn-typed-impl-heads-discriminated.mdk`, carries that axis.
--
-- ⚠️ NOT #1617 (the FUNCTION-typed head, where every stage agreed on None and the
-- fix was to give `TyFun` a tag; here the two projections DISAGREED and the fix was
-- to reconcile them) and NOT #1180 (the bare-`TyVar` arm, where None is intended).
-- The CROSS-MODULE form of this shape behaved identically pre-fix (byte-identical
-- E-PANIC); the single-file form is kept because it is the smaller repro, not
-- because the defect was ever single-file-only.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz (<Stdout> Int) where
  sz _ = 2

main = println (sz 0)
